    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Kutch district in Gujarat is the largest district in India by geographical area, covering 45,674 square kilometers.",
        "Mahe in Puducherry is the smallest district in India, covering an area of only 9 square kilometers.",
        "Serchhip district in Mizoram recorded the highest literacy rate in India at 97.91% according to Census 2011.",
        "Thane district in Maharashtra was recorded as the most populous district in the country as per the 2011 Census data.",
        "Dibang Valley in Arunachal Pradesh has the lowest population density among all districts in India."
      ],
